{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/martinring/tmlanguage/master/tmlanguage.json",
  "name": "Ermine",
  "scopeName": "source.ermine",
  "fileTypes": [
    "e"
  ],
  "_readme": [
    "Derived from the implementation, not from Haskell intuition. The rules that",
    "differ from what you would guess, each verified against a source file:",
    "",
    "  * `--` starts a line comment UNCONDITIONALLY (ParsingUtil.scala:133 \u2014",
    "    `rawWord(\"--\") >> rawSatisfy(_ != '\\n').skipMany`, with a standing TODO",
    "    about operators that start with --). So `-->` is a COMMENT here, not an",
    "    operator, unlike Haskell. StatementExtents.scala says the same thing",
    "    independently. Comments therefore match before operators, on purpose.",
    "  * Block comments NEST (ParsingUtil.scala:134-139).",
    "  * `'` is three things: a char-literal delimiter, an operator character",
    "    (Lexer.opCharSet), and an identifier tail character (Lexer.isTailChar) \u2014",
    "    so `foo'` is one identifier. Identifiers match before char literals, and",
    "    the char rule has a lookbehind so it cannot start mid-identifier.",
    "  * `#` is also both an operator char and a tail char, and one keyword",
    "    (`prj#`) ends in it \u2014 hence the explicit (?![A-Za-z0-9_'#]) guards",
    "    instead of \\b everywhere.",
    "  * An operator may carry a module affix that is PART OF THE LEXEME:",
    "    `++_L` is one token (Lexer.scala header).",
    "  * Three keywords are Greek letters: phi/\u03c6, rho/\u03c1, constraint/\u0393.",
    "  * `if` is a FUNCTION, not a keyword (Bool.e:23-25), and there is no `then`/`else` at all. `'` and `` ` `` are ordinary infix operators (Function.e: infixl 0 ' and infixl 0 `), so the char-literal rule matches only a single character between quotes and never spans.",
    "  * An identifier cannot start with `_` (identTok = letter >> identTail, and `letter` is Character.isLetter); bare `_` is the hole/wildcard. Escapes are \\\\b \\\\f \\\\n \\\\r \\\\t \\\\\\\\ \\\\\" \\\\' and \\\\^X control escapes \u2014 there are NO numeric escapes. Strings may span lines."
  ],
  "patterns": [
    {
      "include": "#comment"
    },
    {
      "include": "#literal"
    },
    {
      "include": "#moduleHeader"
    },
    {
      "include": "#importExport"
    },
    {
      "include": "#fixity"
    },
    {
      "include": "#declarationHead"
    },
    {
      "include": "#keyword"
    },
    {
      "include": "#constructor"
    },
    {
      "include": "#definitionName"
    },
    {
      "include": "#operator"
    },
    {
      "include": "#punctuation"
    }
  ],
  "repository": {
    "comment": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#blockComment"
        },
        {
          "name": "comment.line.double-dash.ermine",
          "match": "--.*$"
        }
      ]
    },
    "blockComment": {
      "name": "comment.block.ermine",
      "begin": "\\{-",
      "end": "-\\}",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#blockComment"
        }
      ]
    },
    "literal": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#literalIdentifier"
        },
        {
          "include": "#string"
        },
        {
          "include": "#date"
        },
        {
          "include": "#char"
        },
        {
          "include": "#number"
        }
      ]
    },
    "literalIdentifier": {
      "name": "entity.name.function.backtick.ermine",
      "begin": "``",
      "end": "``",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "constant.character.escape.control.ermine",
          "match": "\\\\\\^[A-Z]"
        },
        {
          "name": "constant.character.escape.ermine",
          "match": "\\\\."
        }
      ]
    },
    "string": {
      "name": "string.quoted.double.ermine",
      "begin": "\"",
      "end": "\"",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "constant.character.escape.control.ermine",
          "match": "\\\\\\^[A-Z]"
        },
        {
          "name": "constant.character.escape.ermine",
          "match": "\\\\."
        }
      ]
    },
    "char": {
      "name": "string.quoted.single.ermine",
      "match": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_'#])'(\\\\.|[^\\\\'])'"
    },
    "date": {
      "name": "constant.other.date.ermine",
      "match": "@[0-9]+/[0-9]{1,2}/[0-9]{1,2}"
    },
    "number": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "comment": "double/float: digits then a fraction and/or an exponent, optional F suffix",
          "name": "constant.numeric.float.ermine",
          "match": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_'#])[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]*(e[0-9]+)?|e[0-9]+)[Ff]?"
        },
        {
          "comment": "integer with an optional width suffix: L long, B byte, S short",
          "name": "constant.numeric.integer.ermine",
          "match": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_'#])[0-9]+[LlBbSs]?(?![A-Za-z0-9_'#])"
        }
      ]
    },
    "moduleHeader": {
      "begin": "^\\s*(module)\\s+([A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_'#]*(?:\\.[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_'#]*)*)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "keyword.control.module.ermine"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "entity.name.namespace.ermine"
        }
      },
      "end": "(where)|$",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "keyword.control.module.ermine"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#comment"
        }
      ]
    },
    "importExport": {
      "begin": "^\\s*(import|export)(?![A-Za-z0-9_'#])",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "keyword.control.import.ermine"
        }
      },
      "end": "$",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#comment"
        },
        {
          "name": "keyword.control.import.ermine",
          "match": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_'#])(as|using|hiding|type)(?![A-Za-z0-9_'#])"
        },
        {
          "name": "entity.name.namespace.ermine",
          "match": "[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_'#]*(?:\\.[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_'#]*)*"
        },
        {
          "include": "#operator"
        },
        {
          "include": "#punctuation"
        }
      ]
    },
    "fixity": {
      "match": "^\\s*(infixl|infixr|infix|prefix|postfix)\\s+([0-9]+)",
      "captures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "storage.modifier.fixity.ermine"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "constant.numeric.integer.ermine"
        }
      }
    },
    "declarationHead": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "comment": "type-introducing statements: the head word plus the name it binds",
          "match": "^\\s*(data|type|class|instance|field|table|database)(?![A-Za-z0-9_'#])(\\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_'#]*))?",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "storage.type.ermine"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "entity.name.type.ermine"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "storage.modifier.ermine",
          "match": "^\\s*(foreign|private|abstract)(?![A-Za-z0-9_'#])"
        }
      ]
    },
    "keyword": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "comment": "control flow and binding forms. NOT if/then/else: `if` is an ordinary 3-argument function (Bool.e:23) and then/else do not exist in the language (SurfaceParsers.keywords is the authority)",
          "name": "keyword.control.ermine",
          "match": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_'#])(case|of|esac|let|in|do|where)(?![A-Za-z0-9_'#])"
        },
        {
          "comment": "type-level keywords. prj# ends in #, so no \\b; three are Greek",
          "name": "keyword.other.type.ermine",
          "match": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_'#])(forall|exists|constructor|subtype|constraint|rho|phi|prj#|Eval|hole)(?![A-Za-z0-9_'#])|(?<![A-Za-z0-9_'#])[\\u03c1\\u03c6\\u0393]"
        },
        {
          "name": "storage.modifier.ermine",
          "match": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_'#])(foreign|private|abstract|import|export|module|table|field|database|class|instance|data|type)(?![A-Za-z0-9_'#])"
        }
      ]
    },
    "constructor": {
      "comment": "constructors, type names and dotted module paths all start upper",
      "name": "entity.name.type.ermine",
      "match": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_'#.])[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_'#]*(?:\\.[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_'#]*)*"
    },
    "definitionName": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "comment": "a parenthesised operator definition: (++), (prefix !), (postfix !)",
          "match": "^\\s*(\\()\\s*(prefix|postfix)?\\s*([:!#$%&*+./<=>?@\\\\^|~'`-]+(?:_[A-Za-z0-9_'#]+)?)\\s*(\\))",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.parens.ermine"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "storage.modifier.fixity.ermine"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "entity.name.function.operator.ermine"
            },
            "4": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.parens.ermine"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "comment": "a top-level equation or signature head. NOT [a-z_]: identTok is `letter >> identTail` with letter = Character.isLetter, so an identifier cannot START with '_' (bare `_` is the hole/wildcard)",
          "name": "entity.name.function.ermine",
          "match": "^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9_'#]*(?![A-Za-z0-9_'#])"
        }
      ]
    },
    "operator": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "comment": "reserved operators the grammar gives meaning to (Lexer.keyOps)",
          "name": "keyword.operator.reserved.ermine",
          "match": "(?<![:!#$%&*+./<=>?@\\\\^|~'`-])(->|=>|<-|\\.\\.|=|:|~)(?![:!#$%&*+./<=>?@\\\\^|~'`-])"
        },
        {
          "comment": "a user operator, with its optional _Module affix (`++_L` is ONE token)",
          "name": "keyword.operator.ermine",
          "match": "[:!#$%&*+./<=>?@\\\\^|~'`-]+(?:_[A-Za-z0-9_'#]+)?"
        }
      ]
    },
    "punctuation": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "punctuation.section.parens.ermine",
          "match": "[()]"
        },
        {
          "name": "punctuation.section.brackets.ermine",
          "match": "[\\[\\]]"
        },
        {
          "name": "punctuation.section.braces.ermine",
          "match": "[{}]"
        },
        {
          "name": "punctuation.separator.ermine",
          "match": "[,;]"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
